(a) Unless otherwise exempted, any person collecting or transporting scrap tires shall have a scrap tire carrier permit issued by the EPD.
(b) A separate permit shall be required for each scrap tire Carrier business location.
(c) A carrier shall transport scrap tires, properly manifested, only to an end user, recycler, processor, sorter, or disposer approved or permitted by the EPD.
(d) It shall be the responsibility of the carrier to return a completed copy of the manifest to the scrap tire generator, no later than 30 days from the date on which the carrier took possession of the scrap tires, which shall be indicated on the manifest.
(e) The following persons shall not be required to have a scrap tire carrier permit:
(1) Generators who transport scrap tires only between their own branch office locations;
(2) Persons carrying only used tires or retreadable casings;
(3) A tire retailer or tire retreader transporting tires to or from a customer's place of operation or between branch offices of the tire retailer or tire retreader;
(4) A municipal solid waste collector holding a valid solid waste collection permit under authority of EPD Rule 391-3-4-.19 whose primary business is the collection of municipal solid waste;
(5) A private individual transporting the individual's own scrap tires to a processor, permitted disposal facility, or other facility approved by the EPD;
(6) A company transporting the company's own tires to a processor for proper disposal, which company is not in the tire handling business; for example, a soft drink bottler who transports scrap tires generated by the bottler's own vehicle maintenance shop, or a company in the tire handling business who transports only their own scrap tires and which company generates less than 100 scrap tires per month.
a. For the purpose of this paragraph, "tire handling business" means persons whose income is at least partially derived from the sale, processing, transporting, or disposal of tires.
b. Persons who generate less than 100 scrap tires per month and are exempt from having a carrier permit under this section are still required to comply with other applicable provisions of this article.
